import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 954 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 20 | The Law Comes First","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 954 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 20 | The Law Comes First","no":954,"module":5,"tags":["Heavenly-Dao Rule","Rule 20","Law Comes First","Setting Self-Consistency","Law-First Axiom"],"related":["20-Anchor Structure and Hierarchy","906-Law-First Principle","956-Setting Self-Consistency Above Plot Convenience"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0954_模块5-规则二十-法则先行.md","filePath":"en/0954_模块5-规则二十-法则先行.md"}'),n={name:"en/0954_模块5-规则二十-法则先行.md"};function s(r,e,l,h,u,c){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-954-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-20-the-law-comes-first" tabindex="-1">Entry 954 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 20 | The Law Comes First <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-954-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-20-the-law-comes-first" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 954 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 20 | The Law Comes First&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Document 20 | Series: Complete Collection of Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-establish-the-rules-first-then-tell-the-story" tabindex="-1">Introduction: establish the rules first, then tell the story <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-establish-the-rules-first-then-tell-the-story" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: establish the rules first, then tell the story&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law-first axiom is the most easily overlooked yet most decisive of the six top-level axioms. The old cosmos&#39;s laws were &quot;post-hoc ratified&quot;: the plot needs the protagonist to suddenly power up, so a law is temporarily changed; the author needs the villain to suddenly grow strong, so a rule is temporarily loosened. This &quot;laws follow the plot&quot; way of setting ultimately necessarily retcons, ends unfinished, and collapses the worldview. Heavenly-Dao Rule 20 must reverse all this: the law comes first. Any new phenomenon, new plot, or new strong one must first have a legal basis before being allowed to happen in the cosmos; where no law is established, the matter may not be done. This is the law-first axiom&#39;s direct landing at the Heavenly-Dao layer.</p><p>The six top-level axioms here appear as meta-rules: the law-first axiom is this rule&#39;s body; the anti-predation axiom requires the law&#39;s content also be anti-predatory; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires Myriad-Rank participation in law-making; the collective-ascension axiom requires laws serve whole-system ascension; the causal self-discipline axiom requires law changes themselves also be legislated first — any post-hoc law change is void.</p><p>It must further point out the newly added Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a floor basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. This axiom rewrites predation&#39;s meaning at the root: old-cosmos resources and Dao were finite, so predation involution was forced; in Heng Yuan Zhou everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, and predation loses meaning. What this Heavenly-Dao rule establishes is precisely the law guardrail of this new order of &quot;infinite origin, predation meaningless.&quot;</p><h2 id="i-rule-content-three-operations-of-law-first" tabindex="-1">I. Rule Content: Three Operations of Law-First <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-rule-content-three-operations-of-law-first" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Rule Content: Three Operations of Law-First&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Legislate first, act second</strong>: new projects, new institutions, new strong-one posts must first complete law anchoring before operation begins; items unanchored have energy channels closed by the network;</li><li><strong>Interpret first, judge second</strong>: any dispute is first law-interpreted by the Anchor Council, then adjudicated by the Symbiotic Court; &quot;do it first, talk later&quot; is forbidden;</li><li><strong>Calibrate first, expand second</strong>: before the worldview adds planes, clans, or laws, first go through the Terminology Committee and anchor calibration (Document 27), then merge into the main network.</li></ol><p>Law-first is not rigidity: laws may be amended, but amendment must follow the legislative procedure, not &quot;temporarily change when something comes up.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">II. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anchor-structure argument</strong>: the Anchor Structure and Hierarchy (Document 20) points out, of the cosmos&#39;s four-layer structure, the law network lies at the bottom, the base of material planes, the energy layer, and the consciousness domain; an unstable base means upper layers necessarily collapse;</li><li><strong>Retcon-lesson argument</strong>: countless old-cosmos worldviews collapsed because of &quot;plot needs,&quot; their root cause all law-not-first; Heng Yuan Zhou wants a civilization enduring through ages, and must go the opposite way;</li><li><strong>Predictability argument</strong>: Myriad Ranks&#39; evolution needs stable expectations — if laws change order daily, cultivators do not know what to believe, and civilization cannot plan long-term.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-execution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Execution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-execution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Execution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The Alaya Network maintains a &quot;current-law library&quot;; all operations first consult the library: those with basis are released, those without return to the legislative procedure;</li><li>Legislative procedure: Anchor Council proposal → Myriad-Rank representatives&#39; vote → anchor calibration verification → promulgation and effect, fully public throughout;</li><li>The Terminology Committee calibrates new terms and new concepts first, avoiding law ambiguity from &quot;one word, many uses&quot;;</li><li>Newly incorporated cross-plane civilizations&#39; existing laws are first compared, calibrated, and connected with Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s main laws before network merger.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Light</strong>: project already started but laws not fully anchored, make up anchoring within a time limit;</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: under the name of &quot;emergency&quot;/&quot;special&quot; bypassing the legislative procedure to directly change laws, relevant acts are automatically void;</li><li><strong>Heavy</strong>: plot/public opinion/personal will kidnapping laws, post-hoc ratifying illegal operations, handled heavily under Rules 22 and 23 (setting self-consistency, plot does not kidnap).</li></ul><h2 id="v-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">V. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s &quot;law-library verification&quot; is the first layer; the Anchor Supervisory Committee checks &quot;lawless operations&quot; as the second layer; the Symbiotic Court adjudicates &quot;procedural-illegal&quot; cases as the third layer; the Anchor Council itself, as the law-interpretation subject, is reverse-supervised by Myriad-Rank representatives as the fourth layer.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: law-first avoids massive &quot;post-hoc rework&quot; idling; legislating right once saves ten thousand years</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: abolishing at the root the old logic of &quot;the strong are the law&quot;; before the law, strong and commoner are equal; under Axiom 6 everyone inherently possesses basic infinite power, and finite-resource predation loses meaning at the root</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type systems&#39; laws change at Gu Chensha&#39;s whim, powering up on a word; Heng Yuan Zhou laws come first with Myriad-Rank vote, and even the strong cannot temporarily add a clause</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: law-making involves Myriad Ranks, and new laws apply equally to the five lineages</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: the law library supports infinite expansion — new planes, clans, and projects enter via the legislative procedure without collapse</li></ul><p>Law-first must also answer a follow-up: what if the law itself is wrong? The answer is laws may be amended, but amendment must follow the legislative procedure — Anchor Council proposal, Myriad-Rank representatives&#39; vote, anchor calibration verification, promulgation and effect, fully public and traceable. &quot;Wrong so change it&quot; differs from &quot;temporarily change when something comes up&quot; by procedure: the former is Myriad Ranks jointly deciding to retire the old law, the latter is some person or some plot need making the law quietly yield. What law-first protects is not that some law is forever correct, but that &quot;law changes always follow Myriad Ranks&#39; procedure.&quot; This is true endurance through ages.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The law comes first is civilizational finalization&#39;s &quot;meta-rule of rules.&quot; It ensures: no matter how exciting the plot or vast the worldview, the base is forever stable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/20-锚点结构与层级.html">Entry 20 · Anchor Structure and Hierarchy</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/906_模块5-第五条-法则优先原则.html">Entry 906 · Law-First Principle</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/953_模块5-规则十九-根除阶层固化.html">Entry 953 · Rule 19 Eradicate Class Solidification</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/955_模块5-规则二十一-永不吃书永不烂尾.html">Entry 955 · Rule 21 Never Retcon, Never End Unfinished</a></li></ul>',24)])])}const m=t(n,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
